Partition one H821 request on 89e1df4 (issue #44). Slurm job 7743 on
h100-nvl-1-1-cc exposed x86_64 GenuineIntel family 6 model 207, stepping 2,
under KVM. The sampler and the verified process shared logical CPU 0. It
observed one worker. The toolchain was Bend 2.0.40 and Ubuntu Clang 18.1.3.

Apply in a fresh worktree at 89e1df4, then run

    make bootstrap upstream standalone
    f=.upstream/FlashProve/examples/full-size
    model_id=$(cat "$f/ID.txt")
    PATH='' ./build/verify-bend "$f/config" "$f/ivk" "$f/example.req" \
      "$f/example.y" "$f/example.proof" -id "$model_id" -data build -j 1 -timing

On Linux, placing 'taskset -c 0' before 'env PATH=' pins execution to CPU
0 where the scheduler allows it. The instrumented source identity was
6e3c25a2d288784b939009a0c91db4c183913d7aa2c78a3cc3fad9c21aaf433d.
The run returned zero and emitted the four published exact-match lines,
including the build digest and YES. Native process wall time was 86.425 s.

Markers record monotonic wall milliseconds. Starting at request_entry,
take consecutive differences up to request_return and sum by ending marker.
The last row of docs/research/notes/request-outer-timing.tsv is their sum.
This includes logging and destruction of intermediate values. The key
also uses shared and own LIN, so discard every marker before request_entry.
verdict_written follows the existing request timer and is excluded.
The 25 serial links each emit segment_enter, segment_equations,
physical_layout and advance_transport. chain_return includes final BATT.
own_claim assembles the weighted table and masks. own_verify checks
all its FOLD, CS and BASE rounds. The 791 ms at request_return includes
the enclosing request return and releasing its reader, session and trace.

Public inputs took 994 ms, key verification 3616 ms and leaf verification
1454 ms. The request took 80174 ms and the internal whole call 86238 ms.
These diagnostic intervals are from a single successful run on this host.

